S>| clove of garlic (undead will flee)              | 1    |
S>| egg                                             | 1    |
S>| corpse (depends on size)                        | 1-5  |
S>| heavy iron ball                                 | 1-25 |
S>| mirror (also -2 luck)                           | 1    |
S>| potion                                          | 1    |
S>----------------------------------------------------------
S>
S>Finally, all other objects except cameras and cream pies use a weapon damage
S>value based upon their weight (cameras and cream pies cannot do damage):
S>     damage value = weight/10 (minimum of 1, maximum of 6)

So it would seem that statues are in the last category, and would do 
1-6 hit points worth of damage.  A +1 club is better than that.

Unfortuately, this is not quite true.
Nethack code is very tricky.

Statues actually belong to rock_class (like boulders).  Boulders do
1-20 hp when thrown.  However, when wielded, all rock_class things
seem to have a weapon damage of 1-2 (the total damage is this plus
a strength bonus).  

The code which does this is in uhitm.c:

